course: dictionary
lesson: 8504
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. A sardine is a small, silvery sea fish, often eaten from a tin. «They hunt and find sardines, biscuits and a sausage» shows something being eaten, so here sardines means the fish.
explain: The second meaning is an idiom, a phrase whose meaning is different from its separate words. «Packed like sardines» means squashed very tightly together. Nobody is turning into a fish. Ask yourself: does the fish meaning make sense here? If not, try the idiom meaning.
explain: Look at the clues in «sardine tin». A tin is a container, so sardine tin means the tin that small fish came in. Context clues like these help you choose the right meaning quickly, and a dictionary can confirm it.
fact: A sardine is a small, silvery sea fish.
fact: Sardines are often sold in tins and eaten on toast.
fact: Sardines swim in big shoals, and bigger animals eat them.
fact: «Packed like sardines» means squashed very tightly together.
fact: Sardines is also the name of a hide-and-seek game where everyone squeezes into the hiding place.
exercise: «They hunt and find sardines, biscuits and a sausage.» What are sardines here? | *A small, silvery sea fish | A sort of sausage | A kind of biscuit | A hiding place
exercise: The bus was «packed like sardines» at rush hour. What does this mean? | Hungry for fish | Sailing across the sea | *Squashed very tightly together | Very quiet and calm
exercise: «Dietitians suggest eating oily fish, such as salmon or sardines, about once a week.» Salmon and sardines are both examples of what? | Weekly meals only | Tins of food | *Oily fish | Hide-and-seek games
test: The cart was smashed, with «sardine tins scattered over the wide world.» What are the sardine tins? | *Tins that once held small fish | Shiny tins for gold | Tins full of sweets | Empty boxes for cards
test: Mum says, «Our hallway is packed like sardines with coats and bags.» What does she mean? | It has fish in it | It is cold and wet | *It is very crowded and squashed | It is empty and quiet
exam: The word sardine can mean a fish or a squashed crowd. How does context help you choose? | You must look every word up before you read on | *The sentence shows which meaning fits | You should always pick the fish meaning | Context never helps with words that have two meanings
